{
  "findings": [
    {
      "id": "autoloader-generic",
      "level": "warn",
      "places": [],
      "lines": [
        "The app ships no composer/autoload.php, so the server registers its generic loader for lib/ and looks every class up in the file system.",
        "  A composer/composer.json with config.vendor-dir \".\", config.optimize-autoloader true, a config.autoloader-suffix and autoload.psr-4 {\"OCA\\\\OidcClaimMapping\\\\\": \"../lib/\"} makes composer dump-autoload write composer/autoload.php with a class map; the code of the app does not change."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "boot-listener",
      "level": "warn",
      "places": [
        "lib/AppInfo/Application.php:45 get()",
        "lib/AppInfo/Application.php:47 get()"
      ],
      "lines": [
        "boot() registers a listener or takes a service from the container in 2 places. boot() runs once for every process of the server, so each of them is built on every request. registerEventListener() in register() builds a listener only when its event fires.",
        "  lib/AppInfo/Application.php:45 get()",
        "  lib/AppInfo/Application.php:47 get()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "dev-tools-in-root",
      "level": "info",
      "places": [],
      "lines": [
        "vimeo/psalm, phpunit/phpunit are in require-dev of composer.json. The manual recommends a vendor-bin/ of bamarni/composer-bin-plugin per tool, so that the dependencies of a tool cannot conflict with those of the app."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "config-without-lexicon",
      "level": "info",
      "places": [
        "lib/Command/ListRules.php:32 getValueString()",
